--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(B) Third-party / bundled software — NOT covered by the MIT grant
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Lumenora is an OCI/bootc ("image-mode") build layered on the Fedora Atomic
Desktop (Kinoite) base image at `quay.io/fedora-ostree-desktops/kinoite`
(Fedora release 44). The images and ISO it produces are an aggregation of
many independent, individually licensed programs: dozens of upstream RPMs,
Flatpak applications, firmware, and libraries, plus Lumen's own small set of
additions.

This repository cannot and does not relicense any of those components, and
the MIT grant in section (A) does not extend to them. Each component keeps
its own governing license. The authoritative source for any given package is
the license that package declares (an RPM `License:` field, an included
`LICENSE`, `COPYING` or `LICENSES/` file, or the project's own legal pages).
The following list is for clarity; it is illustrative, not exhaustive, and
changes as packages are updated.

- Fedora / core operating-system packages: there is NO single "Fedora
  license". Every package is individually licensed (GNU coreutils
  GPL-3.0-or-later; glibc LGPL-2.1-or-later; systemd LGPL-2.1-or-later;
  and so on).

- Linux kernel: GPL-2.0-only (SPDX `GPL-2.0-only`) with the
  `linux-syscall-note` exception for UAPI / syscall-invoking userspace. It is
  NOT licensed under "GPL v2 or later".

- Open Gaming Collective (OGC) gaming kernel (swapped in by
  `files/scripts/swap-ogc-kernel.sh`): a fork of the Linux stable tree
  (`gregkh/linux`), therefore GPL-2.0-only with the same syscall exception.

- KDE Plasma, KDE Frameworks and KDE Gear: primarily LGPL-2.1-or-later, with
  files also under LGPL-2.1-only, GPL-2.0-only, GPL-2.0-or-later, GPL-3.0-only,
  BSD/MIT, GFDL-1.2 (documentation) and CC-BY-SA-4.0 (media, icons). Individual
  files carry their own SPDX identifiers.

- Qt 6 (which Plasma depends on): LGPL-3.0 or GPL-3.0 for open-source use (not
  LGPL-2.1), under the KDE licensing policy and the
  LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL/GPL licenses.

- NVIDIA driver stack (in the `-nvidia` image variant only): the NVIDIA
  proprietary graphics driver and CUDA runtime are distributed under the
  NVIDIA end-user license agreement (non-free); `nvidia-container-toolkit` is
  Apache-2.0. The `nvidia-open` kernel source flavor (Turing and newer) is
  MIT/NVIDIA licensed. These are added by the build's akmods module, belong to
  their respective owners, and fall outside section (A).

- Other bundled tools (gamescope, MangoHud, GameMode, Steam, the
  `bazaar-store` package set, oh-my-posh, eza, fastfetch, distrobox, flatpaks)
  each carry their own upstream licenses (MIT, BSD, GPL, LGPL, Apache, Mozilla,
  CC, etc.). Flatpak runtime dependencies (e.g. the MangoHud Vulkan layer and
  the freedesktop/GNOME/Qt platform runtimes) carry their own licenses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Distribution obligations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Redistributing or publishing any Lumenora image, ISO, or derivative triggers
the obligations of each bundled component. In particular:

- GPL-2.0-only / GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0 code (e.g. the Linux and OGC
  kernels) must be redistributed in compliance with the GPL, including
  complete corresponding source and license text when redistributed in binary
  form.
- LGPL components (e.g. glibc, systemd, KDE/Qt libraries) permit dynamic
  linking under LGPL; honor re-linking and documentation obligations.
- Apache-2.0, BSD, MIT and other permissive components require preserving
  their notice files.
- Proprietary components (NVIDIA) stay bound by their own license/EULA and must
  not be redistributed beyond NVIDIA's published terms.

This project follows Fedora's legal guidelines for repackaging and
redistribution. The MIT grant above is a claim only over the files Lumen
itself authors in section (A); it is not a claim of ownership over, and
does not relicense, any bundled upstream component. Distributions, derivative
images, or repackages of Lumenora must themselves comply with the licenses of
all bundled components, including GPL source redistribution.